Now I have been using it for some time for my personal projects and at work and I keep using it because it makes real difference! Decisions survive sessions and transfer from different agents. Complex project dependencies are tracked, sudden ideas noted and not forgotten. The code produced with taska is also better. Agents tend to take shortcuts and often leave technical debt intentionally. With taska they file follow up tasks to fix this technical debt before reporting completion, so it gets fixed later instead of being silently lost in long sessions.

